duction of viral proteins associated with hepatitis B virus; Sefaxersen to reduce the production of complement factor B and lower activation of the alternative complement pathway; and Ulefnersen to reduce the production of the fused in sarcoma, as well as other mid-stage pipeline investigational medicines. It has a strategic collaboration with Biogen for the treatment of neurological disorders; and collaboration and license agreement with GSK, AstraZeneca, Novartis, and Roche, as well as with Metagenomi. The company was incorporated in 1989 and is headquartered in Carlsbad, California.","employees":1480,"website":"https://www.ionis.com","country":"United States","city":"Carlsbad","officers":[{"name":"Dr. Brett P. Monia Ph.D.","title":"Founder, CEO & Director"},{"name":"Ms. Elizabeth L. Hougen M.A., M.B.A., M.S.","title":"Executive VP of Finance & CFO"},{"name":"Mr. Patrick R. O'Neil Esq.","title":"Executive VP, Chief Legal Officer, General Counsel & Corporate Secretary"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":18.6,"tpe":30.73,"ps":4.259,"pfcf":27.92,"peg":1.36,"pb":4.405,"ev_ebitda":17.1,"rev_growth":0.0975,"eps_growth":0.1735,"eps_growth_fwd":0.09425,"eps_growth_next":0.1209,"div_yield":0,"roe":0.01671,"roa":0.02187,"de":44.07,"gross_margin":0.4971,"op_margin":0.03985,"profit_margin":0,"current_ratio":3.18},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":-1,"sector":18.6,"verdict":"Loss-making"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":-1,"sector":30.73,"verdict":"Loss-making"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":8.274,"sector":4.259,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":-1,"sector":27.92,"verdict":"Negative FCF"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":null,"sector":1.36,"verdict":"—"},{"k":"pb","label":"Price / Book","v":16.39,"sector":4.405,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"de","label":"Debt / Equity (%)","v":497.8,"sector":44.07,"verdict":"High debt"},{"k":"rev_growth","label":"Revenue growth","v":-0.407,"sector":0.0975,"verdict":"Weak"},{"k":"eps_growth","label":"EPS 